/*
 * Implements semantic validation for calling function-pointer types
 * (FuncPtrType) in Ymir.
 *
 * Responsibilities:
 *   - Reject named parameters(function pointers do not support them).
 *   - Validate argument count against the function pointer signature.
 *   - Infer and validate argument types using CallParamListCreation.
 *   - Perform memory-ownership verification for arguments.
 *   - Compute overload-resolution scoring contributions.
 *   - Construct a FuncPtrCallValue representing the call.
 *
 * This module is invoked by CallMultSymValidation when the selected
 * callable is a function pointer rather than a function declaration,
 * lambda, delegate, or method.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::validator::value::operator::call::fptr
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/validator/value/operator/call/fptr.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-04-25
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
